#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0348-B expect=violation domain=PC
#note "R-5.25 split of SEND348 - the amended rule's own default-row exemplar (top-level-or board wave 2, group J), the PCELTM split sibling: PCELTM is present as a column but not populated on row 1 -> fires, named against this one timing variable instead of the three-name disjunction. Row 2 is populated. Executability stays Partially Executable - Possible Overreporting on every half: the rule cannot tell which PC records contribute to a time-concentration profile."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 PCSEQ=1
dataset PC class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetics Concentrations"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PCSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PCTESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col PCELTM type=Char label="Planned Elapsed Time from Time Point Ref"
---
S1 | PC | 001 | 1 | DRUGX | 
S1 | PC | 001 | 2 | DRUGX | PT0H
